{
  "kanji": "末",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 末\ntitle: end; tip\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 木\nradicalNumber: 75\nonyomi: [マツ, バツ]\nkunyomi: [すえ, うら, うれ]\ndistractors: [未, 本, 木]\n---\n\n# 末 — end; tip\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 木 (no. 75) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n末 names an end or extremity. In time words, it selects the closing part of a period:\n[週末](../words/週末.md) しゅうまつ is the weekend, and 月末 げつまつ is the end of a month.\nThe character can also refer to a physical tip.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** the long top horizontal spreads out at the upper tip of the 木-like shape.\nThis is a memory aid based on the modern form, not a claim about its historical origin.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| マツ | on | [週末](../words/週末.md) しゅうまつ — weekend; 月末 げつまつ — month-end |\n| すえ | kun | 末 すえ — end; tip |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [週末](../words/週末.md) しゅうまつ — weekend\n- 月末 げつまつ — end of the month\n- 年末 ねんまつ — end of the year\n- 末 すえ — end; tip\n\n## Notes\n\nIn 末 the upper horizontal is longer; in [未](未.md) the lower one is longer.\n[本](本.md) has its extra line lower down, while [木](木.md) has only one horizontal.\n末 can name the ending portion of a period; it need not mean only its final instant.\n\nVocabulary: JMdict entries 1333520, 1255840, 1469210 and 1525250.\n",
